# Who may sign a machine-approved refund record.
#
# The signer is the copy gate's reviewer identity: the key that signs outbound-copy
# verdicts on the reviewer host (policies/outbound-copy-reviewer.allowed_signers).
# It is the same key and the same host on purpose - that host is the one place a
# reviewer decision is minted, and node-8 has no copy of the private key, so a root
# process on node-8 can write an approval record but cannot make it an approval.
#
# A DIFFERENT namespace, on purpose: a signature over a copy verdict (namespace
# `muso-outbound-copy-v1`) must never be replayable as a refund approval, so
# `scripts/muso-stripe-write.sh` verifies with `-n muso-refund-approval-v1` and
# `-I outbound-copy-reviewer`. ssh-keygen checks the namespace in this file, so a
# signature minted for the copy gate fails here even with the identical key.
#
# Adding a key to this file is a captain decision: it grants an irreversible
# money path to whoever holds the private half.
outbound-copy-reviewer namespaces="muso-refund-approval-v1" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIC+xcnHfguQO2VCSYUl6TBC++sz1+0O2Pg8Wxu+grxpe
